From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: tdm: establish the ALSA channel map before the first prepare

The HDMI Audio InfoFrame for multi-channel LPCM was transmitted with
channel_allocation = 0 ("FL, FR") for a window at every stream start,
while 6/8-channel audio was already flowing. A sink that latches the
first InfoFrame then decodes the whole title as stereo. The window
length tracks Kodi's videoscreen.delayrefreshchange setting, so it is
configuration-dependent and can reach seconds.

Cause: aml_dai_tdm_prepare() sends the hdmitx audio notify BEFORE it
creates the chmap kcontrol. alsa-lib's snd_pcm_set_chmap() (issued by
Kodi between hw_params and prepare) silently no-ops while the control
does not exist, so the first notify of every stream carries
chmap_layout 0. The control is also destroyed on every playback stop
(commit 221098d0d), so the same happens after every sink rebuild and
XRUN recovery.

Fix:
- create the chmap control at .open, before userspace negotiates, so
  the layout is established when the first prepare sends the notify;
- keep the negotiated layout in struct aml_tdm with an explicit valid
  flag - layout 0 is a legal allocation (2.0), so it cannot double as
  "not established"; only a negotiated layout is ever asserted on the
  wire. Passthrough and unrecognised speaker maps keep CA = 0 exactly
  as before; nothing is derived from the channel count (the table's
  only 4-channel row is 3.1, so deriving would assert 4.0 as 3.1);
- clear the stored layout at open, the real stream boundary, which
  preserves what the stop-time removal was protecting against (a 5.1
  layout leaking into a following stereo or AC3 title via the shared
  CT_PCM InfoFrame path) without depending on it;
- re-attach the control in prepare only as a fallback for a control
  torn down mid-open (XRUN recovery);
- at prepare, assert the stored layout only when its
  channel_allocations[] row matches the stream's current channel
  count, so a client re-running hw_params on one handle can never
  transmit a stale CA (CC=2/CA=0x0b would be the mirror image of the
  bug this fixes);
- guard aml_dai_tdm_chmap_ctl_put() against a closed or unconfigured
  PCM. The control now outlives the stream by design - an enumeration
  open that never starts leaves it registered on a closed PCM - and
  the put dereferenced substream->runtime, so an unprivileged control
  write (amixer cset) on an idle device was a NULL dereference. Same
  guard as the HDA chmap implementation;
- take the card controls write lock around the stop-time
  snd_ctl_remove(), per its documented contract; the dai-links are
  nonatomic so the trigger may sleep.

Also fixed as side effects of moving the state into struct aml_tdm:
the per-stop leak of the kzalloc'd aml_chmap, re-initialisation of a
live mutex on every re-create, and the uninitialised
matches/matched_layout read in the chmap put when the channel count
matches no table entry. The notify log line gains chmap_layout so the
wire value is visible in the journal.

On-box criterion: sampling hdmitx_pkt_dump from playback start, no
sample may show channel_count != 2 with channel_allocation = 0; every
6-channel LPCM notify in the journal must read chmap_layout:0xb.
Stereo and AC3/DTS passthrough must keep CA = 0.

